WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.309 --> 00:00:06.840
Congratulations - you’ve just entered the
employ of the SCP Foundation as a junior researcher!

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:11.210
As you know, the Foundation doesn’t just
hand out positions like this to anyone.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:16.320
To get scouted as part of their Research Corps,
you need to be one of the best and brightest.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:22.039
You’re going to be working with strange,
mind-bending, and sometimes even deadly anomalies

00:00:22.039 --> 00:00:23.169
on a daily basis.

00:00:23.169 --> 00:00:29.740
You’re part of the thin, redacted line between
normalcy and the absolute chaos of the supernatural.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:35.230
But right now, only one question is on your
mind: Where will you actually be working?

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:40.590
Because here’s the thing: The SCP Foundation
is a worldwide organization devoted to the

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:45.760
containment of the anomalous, and they have
thousands of classified Sites and Areas across

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:51.240
the globe, each of them specializing in a
different subset of the strange.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:56.210
Depending on your particular area of expertise,
there’s a number of Foundation facilities

00:00:56.210 --> 00:01:01.250
you may hope to be assigned to, but that’s
not what we’re talking about today, instead

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:05.630
we’re focusing on the Sites and Areas so
dangerous that just getting assigned there

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.890
feels kind of like a demotion to D-Class.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:12.890
The places with the deadliest anomalies and
the most frightening locales.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:18.729
That’s right, it’s time to cross your
fingers and hope for the best, because today

00:01:18.729 --> 00:01:23.749
we’re going to discuss the most dangerous
SCP Foundation Sites and Areas.

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:29.109
But first, there are some things we need to
understand about Foundation facilities in

00:01:29.109 --> 00:01:30.109
general.

00:01:30.109 --> 00:01:33.710
If you’re somewhat familiar with the world
of the SCP Foundation, you’ve probably heard

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:38.979
phrases like “Research Site” and “Biological
Containment Area” thrown around a lot.

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:43.600
You may have even picked up most of the meanings
from context clues, but before we throw you

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:48.690
into even more dangerous uncharted waters,
we’re going to break the labels down for

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:49.690
you.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:53.979
The Foundation has secure facilities all over
the world and they deal with a wide range

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:59.509
of different anomalies, so these facilities
often have to specialize to suit the requirements

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:01.329
of their specific task.

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:05.670
For starters, the terms “Site” and “Area”
aren’t interchangeable.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:11.299
Sites are covert Foundation facilities that
often exist relatively close to civilian populations.

00:02:11.299 --> 00:02:16.349
So as not to arouse suspicion from the public
or rival groups like the Chaos Insurgency,

00:02:16.349 --> 00:02:20.519
they disguise themselves as boring government
and corporate buildings.

00:02:20.519 --> 00:02:26.450
Areas, on the other hand, typically have to
contain much more dangerous anomalies.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:31.780
Areas tend to not only be much larger than
Sites, they’re also further away from civilian

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.209
population centers.

00:02:33.209 --> 00:02:37.750
There’s no cover story here, the Areas are
just entirely hidden.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:43.650
They also often have some pretty crazy fail-safe
measures in case of a large containment breach,

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:48.709
like one or even multiple nuclear warheads
designed to detonate and blow the whole facility

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:52.670
to kingdom come, if things ever get truly
out of control.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:58.360
It goes without saying that you’d probably
rather be assigned to a Site than an Area

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.439
if you’re risk-averse.

00:03:00.439 --> 00:03:05.650
Both types of facilities are divided into
Sections or Sectors, which in some cases are

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:07.989
further divided further into Units.

00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:12.939
Units, typically, are small, high-security
areas devoted to the extensive containment

00:03:12.939 --> 00:03:17.310
of a single anomaly, or several closely related
anomalies.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:23.459
Now that you know the two types of facilities,
let’s talk prefixes - the handy little descriptor

00:03:23.459 --> 00:03:28.609
that often clues you in to how a Foundation
Site or Area has specialized.

00:03:28.609 --> 00:03:33.420
There are ten possible prefixes for a facility,
and we’ll take you on a quick crash course

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.700
through those before we start getting dangerous.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:42.769
“Armed” - as in, Armed Site, Armed Area,
or Armed Section - refers to a facility or

00:03:42.769 --> 00:03:48.250
section that possesses a large quantity of
firepower, and could mean military grade weaponry,

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:52.600
vehicles, or just a large number of permanent
armed guards.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:57.189
Armed facilities tend to be more dangerous
to work in, either due to a greater threat

00:03:57.189 --> 00:04:02.950
of containment breach or due to the high possibility
of attacks from the outside.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:08.090
Biological or “Bio” implies that the facility
or area deals with infectious or biohazardous

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:13.340
anomalies that would make catching the Black
Plague feel like a spa day.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:18.220
Containment is an obvious one - these sites
or areas that are, you guessed it, built for

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:20.680
containing anomalies.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:25.410
Dimensional containment facilities or sections
often contain dangerous pocket dimensions

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.590
or gateways into other dimensions.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:33.319
Humanoid containment facilities or sections
deal largely with intelligent human or human-like

00:04:33.319 --> 00:04:37.630
anomalies capable of understanding and following
instructions.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:42.130
They’re similar to standard prisons, but
for anomalous people.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:47.750
Protected facilities and sections are anomaly-free
safe zones, so we won’t be discussing them

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:49.039
much here.

00:04:49.039 --> 00:04:53.979
Provisional facilities are typically temporary
facilities built around an anomaly that couldn’t

00:04:53.979 --> 00:04:57.660
be feasibly transported to a pre-existing
facility.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:02.630
The rare Reliquary facilities or sections
are designed to hold anomalous artifacts of

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:05.680
a religious or historical nature.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:10.180
Research facilities or sections either research
the anomalies themselves or work on devising

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:15.620
new containment methods, and Storage facilities
are designed to store non-anomalous items

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:16.930
long-term.

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:22.860
The Foundation also has observation outposts
but, with some rare exceptions, your greatest

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.389
risk at one of these is dying of boredom.

00:05:25.389 --> 00:05:30.979
With that out of the way, let’s get to what
we’ve all been waiting for: The scariest,

00:05:30.979 --> 00:05:36.360
deadliest, and most overall dangerous facilities
on the Foundation roster.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:41.460
The places you’d never want to be assigned
to if your life depended on it, and in this

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:43.669
case it really does.

00:05:43.669 --> 00:05:49.670
First, we’ll discuss the most dangerous
sites, and then, the most dangerous areas.

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:53.830
So grab your Foundation-issued sidearm and
let’s go.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.099
First, Site 19.

00:05:55.099 --> 00:05:59.860
It shouldn’t be surprising that the largest
operating Foundation Site is also the one

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:03.070
containing some of its most famous and deadly
prisoners.

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:07.949
Two in particular are the one you can’t
look away from, and another that puts you

00:06:07.949 --> 00:06:11.229
in lifelong mortal danger if you look at it.

00:06:11.229 --> 00:06:18.190
These are SCP - 173, the Sculpture, and SCP
- 689, the Statue of Death.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:23.010
If you get assigned to Site 19, there’s
a possibility you may suddenly find yourself

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:26.410
with a snapped neck while filling in spreadsheets.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:32.111
And if you so much as take a glance at SCP
- 689, you’ll be declared an E-Class, and

00:06:32.111 --> 00:06:35.169
possibly even terminated by your superiors.

00:06:35.169 --> 00:06:43.180
Second, Provisional Site-4511, home of SCP-4511,
also known as The Swine God.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:47.810
This giant, pig-shaped furnace has had a terrifying
effect on the Foundation personnel stationed

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:48.860
at the Site.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:55.060
In just a few weeks, it had seemingly rational
researchers and guards performing brutal sacrifices

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.610
in its name and descending into an occult
hell.

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:03.669
It’s happened at least once already, and
is extremely likely to happen again, so you

00:07:03.669 --> 00:07:06.860
definitely want to avoid being deployed here.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:12.389
But the most deadly site of all is one that
doesn’t even come from our universe: Site

00:07:12.389 --> 00:07:17.789
13, also known as SCP-1730.

00:07:17.789 --> 00:07:22.690
This Site, run by Director Elliot Emerson,
functioned like an anomaly slaughterhouse

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:24.870
in another dimension.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:29.289
Anomalies were murdered and burned, and dissenting
Foundation employees were treated horrifically.

00:07:29.289 --> 00:07:34.461
But when Director Emerson happened to turn
on the reality-warping THRESHER machine, this

00:07:34.461 --> 00:07:40.710
site became a full-blown nightmare filled
with escaped SCPs, memetic hazards, otherworldly

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:48.280
nightmare gods, and a truly unsavoury entity
nicknamed “Leech Boy” who is quite interested

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.240
in drinking your blood.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:54.800
If you can even survive long enough in Site
13 to meet him, that is.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:59.919
Of course, it’s the secure Foundation Areas
where the horrors really unfold.

00:07:59.919 --> 00:08:03.140
These can make some of the worst sites look
mild in comparison.

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:07.819
Let’s take a look at some of the Foundation’s
most dangerous areas.

00:08:07.819 --> 00:08:10.830
First, Containment Area 25b.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:15.189
This Area is not only 200 meters beneath the
ocean, it’s also one of the most heavily

00:08:15.189 --> 00:08:19.949
fortified, and one of the few to actually
detonate its onsite nuclear warhead in the

00:08:19.949 --> 00:08:20.949
past.

00:08:20.949 --> 00:08:28.360
That’s because this is the containment area
for SCP-076, also known as Able.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:33.479
This anomaly has frequent and extremely violent
containment breach attempts, often brutally

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:37.469
slaughtering staff in the process with his
deft swordsmanship.

00:08:37.469 --> 00:08:43.169
Accepting a job here is a great way to fast
track yourself into becoming human sushi.

00:08:43.169 --> 00:08:45.440
Next up is Area-354.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:52.390
This facility houses SCP-354, also known as
the Blood Pond, a slowly expanding pool of

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:57.910
red liquid that habitually unleashes dangerous
monsters that attack the guards stationed

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:58.910
there.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:04.060
These include giant bats, huge metal spheres
releasing concentrated radiation beams, a

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:09.760
giant reptilian humanoid impervious to gunfire,
and an invisible, robotic “Terminator”

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:14.610
entity that managed to murder 90% of the attending
guards before being killed itself.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:19.089
In other words, not a recipe for stable employment.

00:09:19.089 --> 00:09:22.550
Area-126 is dangerous for a number of reasons.

00:09:22.550 --> 00:09:28.529
First, that it’s located inside war-torn
Damascus, Syria, and thus sometimes comes

00:09:28.529 --> 00:09:30.690
under threat from shelling operations.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:35.529
Second, because it contains SCP-3989.

00:09:35.529 --> 00:09:40.480
This spatial anomaly in the middle of an olive
orchard turned out to be a front for a terrifying

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:43.860
Sarkic dimension full of fleshy abominations.

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:50.260
What’s more, simply being in this area slowly
caused the staff to lose their minds and become

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:54.279
devoted to the Sarkic deities hidden within
the dimension.

00:09:54.279 --> 00:09:59.560
And much like the blood pond, it’s believed
that this area of influence is actively growing

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:05.860
day by day, meaning if you work at Area-126
it’s actually getting less safe with each

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.579
moment that passes.

00:10:07.579 --> 00:10:11.760
Next, Armed Reliquary and Containment Area-02.

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:17.170
This base is specifically designed to contain
highly dangerous, hostile, or otherwise hazardous

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:20.050
anomalies, including multiple Keter-class
objects.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:23.930
And we’re not kidding when we say dangerous
and hostile.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:28.980
The anomalies housed on this site are so dangerous
there’s a literal battalion of armed guards

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.490
to keep the peace.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:36.100
It also has not one but multiple fail-safe
nuclear weapons, designed to literally erase

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:41.410
the entire base from existence if ever there’s
a catastrophic containment breach.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:47.339
One particularly horrifying anomaly in Area-02
is SCP-743.

00:10:47.339 --> 00:10:52.160
This is a seemingly innocent chocolate fountain
that actually contains billions of extremely

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:58.110
violent, ant-like creatures that will swarm
anything nearby, tearing it to pieces and

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:02.050
dragging the pieces back to their nest inside
the fountain.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:07.399
These insects will stop at nothing and can
ever tear through titanium if they need to

00:11:07.399 --> 00:11:12.769
in order to get their desired sustenance,
so being present in this Area means your life

00:11:12.769 --> 00:11:14.710
is constantly at risk.

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:16.380
Hope you like chocolate.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:22.020
Next is the dreaded Armed Biological Containment
Area-14, which contains some of the deadliest

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:24.339
biological anomalies out there.

00:11:24.339 --> 00:11:30.519
From the bloodthirsty, kill-crazed heart of
darkness SCP-058, to the head-devouring cannibal

00:11:30.519 --> 00:11:39.300
giant SCP-082, to the voice-imitating, memory
wiping red pack hunters SCP-939.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:44.760
This base also houses several fast-breeding
killer parasites and a few highly infectious

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.710
and deadly diseases.

00:11:46.710 --> 00:11:51.910
While Area-14 does boast an entire army of
guards with heavy military hardware for preventing

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:57.480
all these terrifying monsters from breaching
containment and causing havoc, that probably

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.880
won’t make you feel much better.

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:04.480
If even one of these things escapes at any
given time, you better hope for your family’s

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:08.030
sake that you have a good life insurance policy.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.890
And finally, Area-37.

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:16.339
As it stands, being sent to this area pretty
much guarantees either death or a fate even

00:12:16.339 --> 00:12:17.829
worse than dying.

00:12:17.829 --> 00:12:22.860
That’s because Area-37 is no longer under
the control of the SCP Foundation.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:29.899
Instead, it’s become a twisted playground
for SCP-1765, a trio of terrifying reality

00:12:29.899 --> 00:12:32.760
warpers known as The Sisters.

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:38.089
These unstoppable monsters claimed the Area
as their own and began performing sickening

00:12:38.089 --> 00:12:43.320
experiments, such as being forced into maddening
time loops designed to drive you insane or

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:48.339
being crushed and burned to death in deadly
games with confusing rules.

00:12:48.339 --> 00:12:54.149
While heading into other areas offers the
possibility of a gruesome fate, Area-37 offers

00:12:54.149 --> 00:12:55.550
a dead certainty.

00:12:55.550 --> 00:13:00.910
Now, not only do you now know the difference
between different types of sites and areas,

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:06.959
you now know some of the most horrifying and
deadly examples of each, so you know which

00:13:06.959 --> 00:13:08.100
to avoid.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:12.889
But look on the bright side, if you’re hard
up for work and the SCP Foundation seems like

00:13:12.889 --> 00:13:17.970
an appealing job, at least you know there’ll
likely always be a position available at one

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:19.390
of these sites.

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:23.560
After all, positions here open up very frequently...

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:33.050
Now go check out SCP-4511 The Swine God and
SCP-1765 Sisters for even more on the SCP

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:35.790
Foundation’s deadliest sites and areas.

